  "source_filename": "dhe_2235__lost_and_found_request_form.pdf",
  "slug": "lost-and-found-request-form",
  "title": "Lost and Found Request Form",
  "subtitle": "Take a guest's report of a lost item, describe it well enough to match, and run a search of the areas and storage that could hold it.",
  "description": "An original lost-item report and search request. It captures the claimant and how to reach them, a description detailed enough to match against stored property without prompting, the last-known movements to search, the search performed with results by area, the match decision, unresolved searches, and the handoff to a release order or a closed no-match.",
  "use_case": "Use when a guest reports something missing and the venue needs a description it can match against found property. The request closes when an item is matched and routed to a release order, or the search is exhausted and the claimant is told.",
  "risk_tier": "A",
  "sections": [
